## 3. Rows NOT applied for a checker constraint (noted as the WO requires)
a#50 / b#42 — thousands separator.  ČSN-correct Czech spacing ("500 000", "1 579 589") is REJECTED by
scripts/check-column-translation.mjs: NUMBER_THOUSAND_STYLE.cs = 'dot', and the grouped-number regexes only
accept `.`/`,` groupings, so "500 000 TWD" tokenises as 500 + 0 and "1 579 589 TWD" as 1 + 579 + 589, which
breaks the numbers parity check (verified experimentally with analyzeNumbers before editing). The German-style
dot separators were therefore kept in the columns, per the WO's "prefer the form the checker accepts".
The guidance pack is NOT parsed by that checker, so the team-bio figure there was fixed to Czech form
(1,57 mil. TWD) as a#49 asks. RECOMMENDATION for the supervisor: teach the checker a space/NBSP grouping for
cs/pl/sv/fi/hu/ro/uk before the Czech columns can carry correct Czech number typography.
Dates were fine: "29. 5. 2026" parses to 29/5/2026 in running text, so a#51 was applied.

## 4. Where I disagree with the reviewer (not applied as written)
1. a#35 — gender of the paralegal Fang-Yu Chang. The reviewer infers from the given name 芳瑜 that she is a
   woman and asks for 'Právní asistentka … odpovědná'. The product facts fix only attorney Wei Tseng's gender;
   the canonical record (src/data/team-members.ts) states no gender, and every other gendered locale (pl, ru,
   de …) uses the masculine/neutral form. Guessing a real person's gender from a name is not a fix I am willing
   to ship. I rewrote the sentence so that it carries no gendered participle at all and dropped the redundant
   'paralegal … senior paralegal', which removes the readability complaint without asserting a fact.
   Decision needed from the attorney/supervisor if the feminine form is in fact correct.
2. a#10 / a#9 — link and frontmatter-URL rows: skipped per ACCEPTED-cs, not on my own judgment. One body link
   in 005 still points at the Korean blog with a percent-encoded Hangul slug
   ("…prohloubená část 1" → wei-wei-lawyer.com/post/%EB%8C%80%EB%A7%8C-…). The hard rules forbid changing
   links, so I left it; it could be remapped to /cs/columns/taiwan-company-establishment-advanced-1
   (013 exists in cs) in a follow-up. FLAGGED, not changed.
3. b#27 — the quoted string 'Následující uspořádává obecný pořadí ověření' does not exist in the current
   016 text; the live sentence is already grammatical. The same gender clash in 003 was real and fixed (a#23).
4. a#32/b#40 wording — I did not replace every occurrence of 'porada' with 'konzultace'. 'právní porada' is the
   Czech Bar's own term and reads as good legal Czech; only the calqued compound 'jazyky porady' and the
   'rozhovor' = consultation misuse were replaced. This also keeps guidance-disclosure-parity's cs pattern
   /krokem porady/ and the pinned FAQ 'Je možná porada v češtině?' intact, so no test had to be edited.

